    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1063">

                <pb facs="1036" n="938" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg938"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Griscom.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-02-19"><hi rendition="#italic">February 19,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 211.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose for your convenient information
                    copies of correspondence exchanged between the Department and H. D. Garabedyan,
                    a naturalized Armenian, touching the status of persons of Ottoman origin,
                    naturalized in the United States, who may return to their native country. I also
                    inclose copy of a memorandum on this subject, prepared by Mr. Straus, who is at
                    present in this city.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>




